---
description: Frontend architecture and module-boundary rules.
globs: src/**/*.{ts,tsx}
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use feature-oriented modules under `src/features`.
- Put stable framework-independent types and calculations in `src/domain`.
- Put external integrations in `src/infrastructure`.
- Shared components belong in `src/components` only when they are genuinely reused.
- A component used by one feature stays inside that feature.
- React components must not execute raw Supabase queries.
- Domain calculations must not be embedded in JSX.
- Avoid `any`; model unknown data explicitly and validate external inputs.
- Prefer named exports except where a framework convention clearly benefits from a default export.
- Do not add a global state library without a demonstrated requirement.
- Review components around 250–300 lines, but split by responsibility rather than line count.
- Do not build speculative enterprise abstractions. Keep interfaces only where they protect a real boundary.
